# snap-turn.xrs - snap turn (VR-219): does a push of the right stick step the view AND
# the body by the same fixed angle, once per push, and nothing else?
#
# Needs: a loaded level in GAMEPLAY (not a menu, not the title's attract scene - look
# at an xrsim-shot first), [Mode] GamepadOnly=0, and a build that has the `snapturn`
# word. Run:  .\tools\xrsim-run.ps1 -Path .\tools\xrsim\snap-turn.xrs
# Run it twice, under `movement head` and under `movement character`.
#
# How to read a failure: `snap: FIRED` is the present lane seeing the push; `snap:
# APPLIED` is the script lane writing it into the view; `snap: HONOURED` is the engine
# handing the snapped yaw back on the next dispatch (a verified write is not an
# honoured one). A FIRED with no APPLIED within 500 ms ends in `snap: NO CONSUMER`;
# `snapturn status` prints the lane and why it is blocked. The since-mark numbers come
# from the yaw book (view, body) and the HMD (head): four steps of 30 must read 120 on
# view AND body and about 0 on the head, or the step landed as head yaw, which would
# leave the pawn (and every hit) pointing the old way.

reset
head rot 0 0 0
stick r center
@mod snapturn on; snapturn angle 30; snapturn repeat 0; snapturn threshold 0.6; snapturn rearm 0.3
@wait 800
# `mark` is "start measuring here": it zeroes the counters and the since-mark yaws, so
# the sequence can run again without a relaunch.
@mod snapturn mark
@wait 300
@mark

# 1. One push = one step. Held past the threshold it must NOT repeat (repeat=0).
stick r 0.9 0
@log snap: FIRED \+30 deg
@log snap: APPLIED \+30
@log snap: HONOURED
@wait 500
@nolog snap: FIRED .*hold-repeat
stick r center
@wait 300
@mark

# 2. The second push, after the stick came back under rearm.
stick r 0.9 0
@log snap: FIRED \+30 deg
stick r center
@wait 300
@mark

# 3. Under the threshold: no step, and no smooth turn either (the lane eats RX).
stick r 0.4 0
@wait 700
@nolog snap: FIRED
@modassert features.snapTurn.viewSinceMarkDeg ge 59
@modassert features.snapTurn.viewSinceMarkDeg le 61
stick r center
@wait 300
@mark

# 4. Two more: 4 x 30 = 120 on the view AND on the body; the head did not move.
stick r 0.9 0
@log snap: FIRED \+30 deg
stick r center
@wait 300
stick r 0.9 0
@log snap: FIRED \+30 deg
stick r center
@wait 600
@modassert features.snapTurn.applied eq 4
@modassert features.snapTurn.dropped eq 0
@modassert features.snapTurn.notHonoured eq 0
@modassert features.snapTurn.viewSinceMarkDeg ge 119
@modassert features.snapTurn.viewSinceMarkDeg le 121
@modassert features.snapTurn.bodySinceMarkDeg ge 119
@modassert features.snapTurn.bodySinceMarkDeg le 121
@modassert features.snapTurn.headSinceMarkDeg ge -1
@modassert features.snapTurn.headSinceMarkDeg le 1
# A 30 deg step in one frame is a bigger yaw jump than any smooth turn: both eyes must
# still be fresh at the next submit. (projStaleSubmits is not asserted at the end of this
# file: it is cumulative since launch and climbs through the pause menu in step 7 by
# design, per VERIFICATION's pause-ride note. Measured 2026-09-25: four steps added 0.)
@shot snap_120
@frames 30
@assert eyeAgeL le 0
@assert eyeAgeR le 0
@mark

# 5. A left push steps back.
stick r -0.9 0
@log snap: FIRED -30 deg
stick r center
@wait 400
@modassert features.snapTurn.bodySinceMarkDeg ge 89
@modassert features.snapTurn.bodySinceMarkDeg le 91

# 6. A head turn afterwards moves the view only; the body stays at 90. The sim's
#    `head rot 20` reads as -20 on the mod's HMD yaw (its sign convention), so the
#    view moves the same way: 90 - 20 = 70. A step that had landed as head yaw would
#    fail step 4 above, not this one; this one proves the head still reaches the view.
head rot 20 0 0
@frames 20
@modassert features.snapTurn.bodySinceMarkDeg ge 89
@modassert features.snapTurn.bodySinceMarkDeg le 91
@modassert features.snapTurn.headSinceMarkDeg le -18
@modassert features.snapTurn.viewSinceMarkDeg ge 68
@modassert features.snapTurn.viewSinceMarkDeg le 72
head rot 0 0 0
@frames 20
@mark

# 7. A stick held into and out of the pause menu never fires: the lane is blocked
#    while the menu owns the view, and the stick must come back under rearm first.
@key Escape
@wait 800
stick r 0.9 0
@wait 500
@nolog snap: FIRED
@key Escape
@wait 800
@nolog snap: FIRED
stick r center
@wait 300
@mark

# 8. Off = the game's smooth turn again: the pad line shows RX reaching the game.
@mod snapturn off
@wait 300
stick r 0.9 0
@wait 1300
@nolog snap: FIRED
@log pad/rs: raw=\(0\.90,0\.00\) -> RX=[1-9]
stick r center
@wait 300
@mod snapturn status
